---
import samples from '../../public/data/samples.json';
import '../styles/room.css';
---
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/icons/alexandria-hat.svg"/><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#1b2525"/><meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/><title>Alexandria Library · A listening library</title><meta name="description" content="A quiet research tavern. Open a paper, hear the conversation, keep the idea."/></head><body>
<header><a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Alexandria Library home"><img class="brand-hat" src="/icons/alexandria-hat.svg" alt=""/><span>Alexandria Library</span></a><span class="small">A listening library for curious minds</span><label class="device-view-label" for="device-view">View <select id="device-view" aria-label="Choose device view"><option value="auto">Auto</option><option value="phone">Phone</option><option value="computer">Computer</option></select></label><button id="settings-open" aria-label="Open library settings">⚙</button></header><div id="pip-home"></div><aside class="familiar" id="familiar" aria-label="Pip, your floating librarian"><button id="pip-handle" class="pip-handle" aria-label="Pip: drag to move, click to hide or show his message" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="pip-speech"><span class="cat" id="cat" role="img" aria-label="Pip, your animated wizard cat"></span></button><div class="speech" id="pip-speech"><strong>PIP · YOUR FAMILIAR</strong><p id="cat-message" aria-live="polite">Pick a spine and I’ll keep you company. You can drag me anywhere — I’ll stay with you as you scroll.</p><div class="pip-guide-actions"><button id="tour-start">Show me around</button><button id="tour-next" hidden>Next →</button><button id="tour-stop" hidden>Finish tour</button></div></div></aside>
<main>
<div class="room"><div class="window" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>✧</span></div><div class="candle left" aria-hidden="true">🕯</div><div class="candle right" aria-hidden="true">🕯</div>
<section class="bookcase" aria-label="Research bookshelf"><div class="carving">☾ &nbsp; THE COLLECTED CURIOSITIES &nbsp; ✧</div>
{['finance','quantum'].map((shelf)=><div class="shelf"><div class="shelf-heading"><div class="shelf-label">{shelf==='finance'?'I · QUANTITATIVE FINANCE':'II · QUANTUM PHYSICS & COMPUTING'}</div><button class="shelf-generate" data-generate-shelf={shelf}>{shelf==='finance'?'✦ Generate finance podcast':'✦ Generate quantum podcast'}</button></div><div class="books">{samples.filter(p=>p.shelf===shelf).map((paper)=><button class={`book book-${paper.index}`} data-id={paper.id} aria-label={`Open ${paper.title}`}><span class="book-number">0{paper.index+1}</span><span class="spine-title">{paper.shortTitle}</span><span class="spine-star">✧</span><time class="book-date" datetime={paper.published}>{new Date(paper.published).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{day:'2-digit',month:'short',year:'numeric',timeZone:'UTC'})}</time><span class="book-foot">PAPER + PODCAST</span></button>)}<div class="shelf-object" aria-hidden="true">{shelf==='finance'?'◈':'⚗'}</div><div class="leaning" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><div class="wood-edge"></div></div>)}
<div class="case-bottom"><button id="latest-open">↻ New arrivals</button><button id="upload-open">＋ Add a paper</button><button id="offline-open">↓ Offline books</button><button id="shared-open">♫ Library episodes</button><span>5 volumes · archival collection</span></div></section>
<div class="rug" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
<footer><span>Made for slow listening & bright ideas.</span><span>arXiv sources · Human curiosity · AI voices disclosed</span></footer></main>
<dialog id="reader"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close book">×</button><div class="open-book"><div class="cover-page"><p id="reader-shelf" class="eyebrow"></p><div id="cover" class="manga"></div><h2 id="reader-title"></h2><p id="authors"></p><a id="paper-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the original paper ↗</a><p class="fine" id="cover-note">Conceptual manga artwork. Not a scientific diagram.</p><details id="comic-details"><summary>Unfold the research comic</summary><img id="comic" class="comic" src="/art/research-manga-panels-v2.png" alt="Five conceptual pixel manga scenes: learning agents, simulated markets, visibility graphs, quantum option pricing, and quantum noise"/><p class="fine">Scenes follow the five archival conversations. Artistic interpretation, not a depiction of measured results.</p></details></div><div class="reading-page"><p class="eyebrow">THE FIRESIDE CONVERSATION</p><h3 id="episode-title"></h3><p id="episode-note" class="fine"></p><audio id="audio" controls preload="metadata"></audio><div class="reader-actions"><button id="transcript-toggle">Read transcript</button><button id="email-open">Send this book</button><button id="offline-save">Keep offline</button></div><div id="transcript" hidden></div><details><summary>Make a fresh two-host episode</summary><label>Length <output id="minutes-value">10</output> minutes<input id="minutes" type="range" min="5" max="25" value="10"/></label><button id="generate">Queue episode</button><p class="fine">AI voices: Mira & Sol. Requires configured cloud services. Supplied audio above is an existing recording.</p></details><div id="quiz" hidden><h3>Pip’s three little questions</h3><p class="fine">Based on this recording’s automatic transcript. Seeking to the end opens this too.</p><form id="quiz-form"></form><div id="quiz-result" aria-live="polite"></div><form id="feedback"><label>How difficult was it? <output id="difficulty-value">3</output><input type="range" name="difficulty" min="1" max="5" value="3"/></label><label>How useful? <output id="usefulness-value">3</output><input type="range" name="usefulness" min="1" max="5" value="3"/></label><button>Save & guide my next read</button></form></div><p id="reader-status" role="status"></p></div></div></dialog>
<dialog id="generation" aria-labelledby="generation-title"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close podcast generation">×</button><p class="eyebrow">FROM ARXIV TO THE FIRESIDE</p><h2 id="generation-title">Generate a podcast</h2><p id="generation-catalogue-status" role="status">Checking the latest papers…</p><form id="generation-form"><fieldset id="generation-papers"><legend>Choose one of the latest five papers</legend></fieldset><label>Episode length: <output id="generation-minutes-value">10</output> minutes<input id="generation-minutes" name="minutes" type="range" min="5" max="25" value="10"/></label><p class="fine">Mira &amp; Sol · two AI voices. Generation uses your configured cloud provider and durable worker. Papers are research, not proof of trading profit.</p><button id="generation-submit" disabled>Generate podcast</button></form><p id="generation-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="reader-actions"><button id="generation-key">Library connection</button><button id="generation-jobs">Check generation jobs</button></div><p class="fine">One shared backend, managed by the library owner. No personal database or API key is needed.</p></dialog>
<dialog id="email"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close email form">×</button><h2>A book, by owl post.</h2><form id="email-form"><label>Your email<input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" maxlength="254"/></label><p class="fine">Sends a source link to this address only when you press send.</p><button>Send this book</button></form><p id="email-status" role="status"></p></dialog>
<dialog id="settings"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close settings">×</button><h2>Your shared library</h2><p>This app uses the library owner’s Supabase backend. You never need your own database or API keys.</p><p id="library-status" role="status">Checking the library connection…</p><button id="shared-from-settings">Browse library episodes</button><details><summary>Owner controls</summary><p class="fine">Only the owner configures Supabase, generation and email on the server. Visitors should not enter any credentials.</p><label>Owner access token<input id="owner-token" type="password" autocomplete="off"/></label><button id="save-token">Use owner key</button><button id="jobs-open">Owner generation jobs</button><div id="jobs" role="status"></div></details></dialog>
<dialog id="latest"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close new arrivals">×</button><h2>New arrivals</h2><p id="catalogue-status">Checking the catalogue…</p><details><summary>Five research prompts from the latest finance papers</summary><div id="brief"></div></details><div id="catalogue"></div><p class="fine">Checks every three hours when a scheduler is connected. arXiv publishes on its own schedule. Research hypotheses require testing, costs and out-of-sample validation.</p></dialog>
<dialog id="upload"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close upload">×</button><h2>A place for your paper</h2><p>PDF drafts are kept privately in this browser. You can also paste source text to queue cloud generation.</p><form id="upload-form"><label>PDF (up to 20 MB)<input type="file" name="pdf" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" required/></label><label>Title<input name="title" required maxlength="200"/></label><button>Keep a local draft</button></form><p id="upload-status" role="status"></p><div id="drafts"></div><details><summary>Generate from your paper’s text</summary><form id="source-form"><label>Title<input name="title" required maxlength="200"/></label><label>Shelf<select name="shelf"><option value="finance">Finance</option><option value="quantum">Quantum</option></select></label><label>Extracted source text<textarea name="text" required minlength="100" maxlength="100000" rows="8"></textarea></label><button>Upload text & queue 10-minute episode</button><p class="fine">Explicitly uploads this text to your private cloud store and generation provider.</p></form></details></dialog>
<dialog id="offline-library"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close offline library">×</button><h2>Your pocket library</h2><p>Saved on this device. Download while online before travelling, then test playback in airplane mode.</p><div id="offline-list"></div><p id="offline-status" role="status"></p><button id="offline-test">Test offline mode</button><details><summary>Use this on your phone</summary><p>Open the hosted HTTPS app on your phone while online. In Safari, Share → Add to Home Screen; in Chrome, use Install app or Add to Home Screen. Open the installed app online once, then save each episode there with Keep offline.</p><p>Localhost is only this computer. Storage can be cleared or evicted by the browser. New generation, arXiv refresh and email require a connection.</p></details></dialog><dialog id="shared-library"><button class="close" data-close aria-label="Close library episodes">×</button><h2>Library episodes</h2><p id="shared-status" role="status"></p><div id="shared-episodes"></div></dialog><script define:vars={{samples}}>window.__papers=samples;</script><script src="../client/room.js"></script><script src="../client/device-view.js"></script></body></html>
